(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #120 - the fix skips a single line break before an
 instance/type possessive call's preposition, but must not over-reach: a
 blank line (paragraph break) still force-closes the sentence, same as
 everywhere else in the language, so `of 2.` below is refused as its own
 unfinished statement.)

A thing called point has
  a number called x is 0,
  a number called y is 0.

To 'scaled' with a point called corner and a number called factor.
  Return a number, corner's x multiply factor.

a point called origin.
Set origin's x to 3.
a number called c1 is origin's 'scaled'

    of 2.
Print c1.
